        "context": "Table 5 (\"Impact of Ownership Type on Earnings and Earnings Distributions\"), column 1.  Regression discontinuity at the 1980 land reform's 500 ha cumulative-landholding threshold: properties of former owners above 500 ha became worker cooperatives, those below stayed outside-owned haciendas.  Outcome: household earnings per capita in the previous month, in dollars per month, of agricultural workers in the El Salvador household surveys (Encuesta de Hogares de Propositos Multiples, 2002-2013), matched to cooperatives and haciendas through the survey's questions on working as a cooperative member or hacienda laborer (matching limited to cantons with only one cooperative/large hacienda).  Regressor: Above500, an indicator for the property's former owner having over 500 ha in cumulative landholdings in 1980.  Linear control in the former owner's total landholdings estimated separately on each side of the cutoff (equation 1), sample limited to properties within 300 ha of the threshold, survey-round fixed effects, standard errors clustered at the former-owner level.  Observations are workers; the table also reports the number of properties, the number of clusters and the mean of the dependent variable.\n",
